{"type":"theorem","type_name":"Theorem","number":"18.9.5","title":"Minkowski–Weyl Theorem","title_html":"Minkowski–Weyl Theorem","html":"<div class=\"enumerate\" data-options=\"label=(\\alph*)\">\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>A subset of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}^n\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is a polytope\nif and only if it is a bounded polyhedron.</li>\n<li>A subset of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}^n\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msup><mjx-TeXAtom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-ds mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c211D TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-TeXAtom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is a finitely\ngenerated cone if and only if it is a polyhedral cone.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch18-convexity/09-polytopes.html"}